<detour title="cache-aside"/>That's the cache-aside pattern. <node id="api" label="API"/><node id="redis" label="Redis" kind="db" near="api"/><edge from="api" to="redis" label="hit" style="dashed"/>Reads go to Redis first. <code path="./internal/user/service.go" lines="42–52"/>Here is the code. <line n="44"/>On a miss <trace path="api>redis"/>it goes on. <annotate target="redis" mark="underline" text="TTL"/>Watch the TTL. <strike target="redis" text="Valkey"/>Well, Valkey now. <compare options="Redis|Memcached" criteria="Latency|Persistence"/>Two options. <cell row="Redis" col="1" mark="yes"/><cell row="1" col="Persistence" text="no disk"/>One persists. <close surface="all"/><resume/>So, back to the request. <node id="vpc" label="VPC" kind="group"/><node id="db" label="Postgres" kind="db" in="vpc"/>The database lives in the VPC.
